      "summary": "The intake routes PDFs through the child worker, and the tests cover the listed parser cases. The memory limit is enforced by periodic sampling rather than a cap, leaving a reachable path for a decompression spike to exceed the limit before the worker is killed.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Evidence/IsolatedPdfParser.cs",
          "line": 208,
          "message": "The sampled working-set check does not enforce the required hard memory limit; a rapid decompression allocation can exceed 512 MB before the parent observes it.",
          "confidence": 0.81,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "Supervise checks the child's working set only between 25 ms waits, then kills it if the sampled value exceeds the configured limit. No OS memory limit caps the child during that interval.",
            "failureScenario": "A crafted PDF whose decompression causes a rapid allocation spike can push the child well past 512 MB before the next working-set sample. The child can consume enough memory to exhaust the service host before the parent kills it, contrary to the hard memory-limit criterion."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
